From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fexiven <48439988+Fexiven@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:58:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 20/23] rocket: rk3576: fold a PAD into a first convolution

YOLOX pads its 416x416x3 input image by one pixel before the 3x3
stride 2 VALID first convolution. Such a PAD (<= 4 channels) was left to
the CPU, where TFLite's PAD takes 1.8 ms for this image, and the NPU
partition started behind it.

The first-convolution encoder already programs explicit padding (0x1080)
with the input zero point as the pad value (0x1084, 0x1070 for the raw
int8 input), as the SAME first convolutions of the other models use. So
a small-channel PAD is folded like the larger ones: the convolution reads
the PAD's input, in the tight first-convolution layout the CPU uploads,
with the PAD added to its own padding.

rkt_ml_operations_filter() keeps such a PAD only when every consumer is
a convolution the first-conv encoder takes (rkt_fc_any_shape), and the
tight-input rule looks through a folded PAD at its input.

YOLOX: 18.1 -> 16.4 ms, outputs byte-identical. Test models with a PAD
of 0 to 3 pixels per side in front of 1- and 3-channel convolutions
(k 3/5/7, stride 1/2, first-conv modes 2 and 6) are byte-identical to the
CPU PAD.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C6ragSxZN7WKWgGsfgrMX1
---
 src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c
index d8cebfb..b81c30e 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/rocket/rkt_ml.c
@@ -1025,8 +1025,13 @@ rkt_pad_supported(const struct pipe_ml_operation *operation)
    if (i->scale != o->scale || i->zero_point != o->zero_point ||
        i->is_signed != o->is_signed)
       return false;
-   if (operation->pad.before_z || operation->pad.after_z || i->dims[0] != 1 ||
-       i->dims[3] <= 4)
+   /*
+    * <= 4 channels: the input of a first convolution, which reads the PAD's
+    * input in its tight layout with the padding in its CNA registers
+    * (rkt_ml_operations_filter() checks that the consumers are such
+    * convolutions).
+    */
+   if (operation->pad.before_z || operation->pad.after_z || i->dims[0] != 1)
       return false;
    /* the CNA pad fields: up to 7 per side together with the conv's own */
    if (operation->pad.before_x > 4 || operation->pad.after_x > 4 ||
@@ -1368,6 +1373,17 @@ drop_misplaced(struct rkt_ml_graph *g, bool *supported)
             if (j != 0 || !supported[k] || g->partition[k] != g->partition[i] ||
                 ops[k].type != PIPE_ML_OPERATION_TYPE_CONVOLUTION)
                ok = false;
+            /*
+             * a small-channel PAD: only the first-conv encoder takes the
+             * padding, whatever the convolution's input width
+             */
+            else if (out->dims[3] <= 4 &&
+                     !rkt_fc_any_shape(out->dims[3],
+                                       ops[k].conv.weight_tensor->dims[1],
+                                       ops[k].conv.weight_tensor->dims[2],
+                                       ops[k].conv.stride_x,
+                                       ops[k].conv.depthwise))
+               ok = false;
          }
       }
       if (!ok || !consumers) {
@@ -1382,18 +1398,26 @@ drop_misplaced(struct rkt_ml_graph *g, bool *supported)
     * therefore not come from another claimed operation (it would be
     * written in the NC1HWC2 layout) nor feed a claimed operation that is
     * not such a convolution. The first convolution of a model reads the
-    * graph input and keeps it.
+    * graph input and keeps it, also through a PAD folded into it.
     */
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
       const struct pipe_tensor *t;
+      int pad = g->producer[i][0];
 
       if (!supported[i] || !tight_small_input(&ops[i]))
          continue;
       t = ops[i].input_tensors[0];
+      /* a PAD folded into the convolution: it reads the PAD's input */
+      if (pad >= 0 && supported[pad] && g->partition[pad] == g->partition[i] &&
+          ops[pad].type == PIPE_ML_OPERATION_TYPE_PAD)
+         t = ops[pad].input_tensors[0];
+      else
+         pad = -1;
       for (int k = 0; k < n; k++) {
          bool reads = false, writes = false;
 
-         if (k == i || !supported[k] || g->partition[k] != g->partition[i])
+         if (k == i || k == pad || !supported[k] ||
+             g->partition[k] != g->partition[i])
             continue;
          for (unsigned j = 0; j < ops[k].output_count; j++)
             writes |= ops[k].output_tensors[j] == t;
